==Strategy==
You'll have to bring a lot of good area attackers, a shield piercer for the Aku Cyclone, and crowd-controllers (e.g. [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Master Uril]], [[Medusa Cat (Rare Cat)|Naga Cat]]) for the Primeval Cyclone. Slapsticks are essential, able to deal great damage in general, being strong against Relics and have enough range to handle the peons, though support from other attackers like Cameramen and Can Can or even Ubers are greatly appreciated. The Sir Seals will be your main source of money.

While the two Cyclones don't spawn together, you can't waste any time on brute forcing Aku Cyclone's shield with the strong peons in the way, and your main goal is to take it down as soon as possible. Shield piercers such as [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Aku Researcher]] or [[Talents|Talented]] [[Li'l Gross Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Macho Legs]] can work wonders here, but do not use Supercar since Aku Cyclone outranges it. Since [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|dual]] [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Erasers]] can effectively stall Aku Cyclone, they are also recommended here. [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]] is also a great meatshield option as it is resistant against both cyclones.

